# =====================================================================
#  What is NOT in this repository, and why.
#
#  The working tree is around 180 MB; the source and the documents that
#  describe it are about 2 MB. Everything else here is a build product, a
#  machine-local snapshot, or a screenshot dump -- and all of it can be
#  regenerated from what IS committed:
#
#      build/         rebuilt by scripts\build.ps1 (54 MB)
#      backups/       timestamped local snapshots from scripts\snapshot.ps1 (15 MB)
#      captures/      frame dumps written by the app while it runs (28 MB)
#      docs/*.png     screenshots; the drawings they show come from the source
#
#  The PNGs are the awkward case. They are genuinely useful -- they are how
#  the panel's layout was verified against what the shell does -- but 204 of
#  them are 80 MB, and a repository that takes a minute to clone is a
#  repository nobody clones. They stay on the machine. If a screenshot is
#  needed to explain something, attach it to the issue or the release, where
#  it costs the clone nothing.
#
#  Getting this right BEFORE the first commit is the whole point: a file
#  that has been committed stays in the history for ever, and taking it out
#  later rewrites every commit that followed.
# =====================================================================

# --- build output -----------------------------------------------------
build/
.zig-cache/
.zig-global-cache/
.zig-cache-*/
.zig-out*/
zig-out/
island/zig-out/
island/*.stdout.txt
island/*.stderr.txt
out/
[Oo]ut/
*.obj
*.o
*.exe
*.dll
*.lib
*.exp
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.idb
*.res
*.tlog
*.lastbuildstate
*.log
.vs/
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
*.vcxproj*
*.sln
CTestTestfile.cmake

# --- local snapshots and runtime dumps --------------------------------
backups/
captures/
island/backups/
island/captures/

# --- screenshots ------------------------------------------------------
# Screenshots are kept under docs/screenshots for local review, not committed.
docs/screenshots/
docs/*.png
docs/*.jpg
docs/*.jpeg
docs/*.gif
docs/*.bmp

# --- scratch files ----------------------------------------------------
# Written while diagnosing something; they are empty or machine-specific.
selftest_check.txt
trace.txt
__st.txt
appbar-run.log
*.tmp
*.bak
*~

# --- editors ----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.user
*.suo
*.swp
